<urn:atm:triage:finding/CPR-016>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "CPR-016" ;
  triage:title "An undeliverable queue item permanently silences that member's task reminders (absorbs CPR-005)" ;
  triage:description "Hostile closure review (general-purpose opus, task af4edaf6699568f49) @ 9f5aef2fe. An undeliverable queue item permanently silences that member's task reminders. Doc says: nudge-task-design.md §1: 'Up until the point a task is complete the agent MUST keep working on it.' Code does: dispose returns Hold('mail pending') whenever any open queue item exists for the member. An item that can never be delivered or read (no delivery channel, dead pane, permanently unreachable transport) stays open forever, so the member's task nudges are suppressed indefinitely with no escalation. Recommendation: Bound the mail-pending hold: after N consecutive holds on the same item, escalate or fall through to the task nudge. fenix's ruling: a queue prompt to a member with an open head task counts as a reminder against the same section-6 counter -- this closes both the frozen reminder_count problem (CPR-005) and the unbounded mail-pending hold (CPR-016) with one counter change. ALSO ABSORBS CPR-005 (reminder_count frozen on the primary assignment flow): Hostile closure review (general-purpose opus, task af4edaf6699568f49) @ 9f5aef2fe. reminder_count is frozen on the primary assignment flow, so a real assignment can never reach the escalation threshold. Doc says: nudge-task-design.md §6: reminders accumulate and escalate terminally at TASK_STALLED_REMINDER_THRESHOLD = 10. Code does: Assignments always set requires_ack (crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs:348-356: `task_id.is_some() && request.task_op.is_none()`), so the assignment message stays an open queue item until acked or closed. dispose therefore returns Hold('mail pending') every tick and no task reminder is recorded. After Start, complete_task_handoff_if_head filters `row.state == TaskState::Assigned && position == 1`, so the reminder-recording handoff no longer runs either. Recommendation: Decide whether the assignment message's open-queue state should suppress task reminders at all; if not, exclude the task's own assignment message from the mail_pending computation in dispose. Add an end-to-end test that drives reminder_count from 0 to 10 through the real pump." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_task_disposition.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix (ATM 01M2AAHXS8QB8CQTR4J0BSHVST, 2026-09-12T08:08:16Z): fixed at review-2 a719f8955, chain b337cdfce (counter) + 8f3dfcc40 (own-assignment handoff guard) + a719f8955 (dead-flag cleanup); all gate-green on fenix's host. Closes both CPR-016 and CPR-005 with one counter change. quality-mgr consolidated QA (BA-REVIEW-QA-1789194730, PR #1425 comment 5645308114, 2026-09-12T10:24:25Z): the counter-freeze aspect (ex-CPR-005) is confirmed fixed, but the original unbounded-mail-pending-hold aspect remains -- an undeliverable/retry-exhausted queue item still leaves dispose()'s Hold(\"mail pending\") unbounded with no escalation fallback once permanently unclaimable; pending_nudge_store.rs test comment cites ADR-054(f) as the accepted current behavior (team-lead confirmed the ADR-054(f) comment exists at crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/pending_nudge_store.rs:905). Reopened as post-landing backlog (Important); the reminder-counter closure stands." ;
  triage:relatedFinding "CPR-005" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/CPR-016/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/CPR-016/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/CPR-016/3> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "3" .

